  "summary_en": "Opinion of the German Ethics Council on robotics in care for older people and severely disabled people. It analyses ethical issues at micro, meso and macro levels of responsibility and holds that robots should complement, not replace, human care. It issues recommendations on safety, liability, participation, institutions and training.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robots must complement, not substitute, interpersonal care; only persons bear moral responsibility.",
   "Strict safety standards, approval rules, strict liability, reversed burden of proof and insurance; legislators should review medical device and liability law.",
   "Ethics and participatory design from early development stages, including affected users and carers.",
   "Care facilities must maintain robots and ensure ongoing care indication; evidence of improved care quality is required before standard coverage.",
   "Nursing curricula and continuing training should include new technologies and their ethics."
  ],
